Subject: OPL player: no GENMIDI lump means no OPL music, not a fatal error

The Macintosh Hexen CD's Hexen.WAD (21078584 bytes) is the 1.1 game but
has no GENMIDI and no DMXGUS lump. LoadInstrumentTable() fetched GENMIDI
with W_LumpByName(), which stops the game ("W_GetNumForName: GENMIDI not
found", exit 255) even when another music player is selected. It now
returns false when the lump is missing; I_OPL_InitMusic() already shuts
the OPL down and reports failure then, so OPL music is unavailable and
the other players (fluidsynth, SDL mixer) are unaffected.

Forwarded: not yet (candidate for upstream)

diff --git a/prboom2/src/MUSIC/oplplayer.c b/prboom2/src/MUSIC/oplplayer.c
--- a/prboom2/src/MUSIC/oplplayer.c
+++ b/prboom2/src/MUSIC/oplplayer.c
@@ -375,6 +375,13 @@ static dboolean LoadInstrumentTable(void)
 {
     const byte *lump;
 
+    // A WAD without GENMIDI (the Macintosh Hexen CD's) has no OPL
+    // instruments: the OPL player is unavailable, the game runs.
+    if (!W_LumpNameExists("GENMIDI"))
+    {
+        return false;
+    }
+
     lump = (const byte*)W_LumpByName("GENMIDI");
 
     // Check header
